  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 237 AM EDT Mon Jul 20 2026\n\n- Thunderstorms Tonight With Damaging Winds Possible\n\nPrimary concern with this forecast package is for the potential of \nsevere thunderstorms tonight. A cold front looks to trigger storms \nacross the upper midwest this afternoon which progresses eastward \nMonday evening. Questions remain as to the strength of any \nconvection, with timing favored to be late this evening into the \nearly overnight hours.\n\nEvaluation of forecast profiles suggests the potential for an MCS on \nthe nose of a 40 kt LLJ, with strong low-level and deep layer shear. \nThis lends itself to a primary threat of damaging winds, with large \nhail in any discrete convection given steep mid-level lapse rates. \nInstability looks to be sufficient as well (albeit waning with \neastward extent), so even with uncertainties as to convective \nstrength, the environment warrants the Slight (Level 2/5) risk in \nplace across most of the CWA. The threat ends Tuesday morning as the \ncold front exits the CWA.\n\n- Dry and Cooler Mid to Late Week\n\nTuesday through late week will feature a relatively stable pattern \nwith persistent upper-level troughing and surface ridging across the \narea. Combined with the dry airmass, dry conditons are favored at \nthis point. Look for highs in the 70s mid-week climbing back into \nthe low 80s by the weekend.",
